{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDAwLS0yMDEwL0p1c3QlMjBNYXJyaWVkJTIwJTI4MjAwMyUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Just Married","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/FRqnYDjbstsCgLSJJ3SifOh2ca.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/4ZnoQNulHriHTqanH55OlldYYuX.jpg","description":"Although Tom Leezak and Sarah McNerney come from different worlds, they are both unexpectedly swept off their feet after their first meeting. They quickly fall in love and plan to get married, despite opposition from Sarah's uptight, rich family. After their wedding, the happy couple sets off - with the highest of hopes and ideals about love and marriage - on what they expect will be the perfect honeymoon in Italy. Thanks to a relentless string of bad luck with one disaster after another, and an impromptu visit from Sarah's wealthy one-time ex-lover Peter Prentiss, the newlyweds experience the honeymoon from hell that tests the limits of their young love.  Is it worth throwing away their love and marriage?\n\nRated PG-13 · Released 8 Jan 2003 · Germany, United States of America · Language: English · 95 min\nStudio: Robert Simonds Productions, 20th Century Fox, Mediastream Dritte Film\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2003","genres":["Romance","Comedy","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"5.8","runtime":"95 min","cast":["Ashton Kutcher","Brittany Murphy","Christian Kane","David Moscow","Monet Mazur","David Rasche","Thad Luckinbill","David Agranov"],"director":["Shawn Levy"],"released":"2003-01-08T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"It was the perfect honeymoon...until it began.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Shawn Levy","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/x7dJcZeemLlgRB2eHlBG60WFc2Q.jpg"},{"name":"Ashton Kutcher","character":"Tom Leezak","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/qJlM29jTncF9GpmE0PPVwbp5iPB.jpg"},{"name":"Brittany Murphy","character":"Sarah McNerney","photo":"https://i